WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.567
-Our next guest can be seen

00:00:02.567 --> 00:00:05.000
this Friday and Saturday
at Laugh Boston.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.100
Please welcome
the very funny Ian Lara!

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:10.701
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:17.634
-Hey, hey, hey.

00:00:17.634 --> 00:00:19.834
This is very nice.
I'm very excited to be here.

00:00:19.834 --> 00:00:22.634
I just celebrated
my 33rd birthday.

00:00:22.634 --> 00:00:26.267
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah. Yeah, it's nice.

00:00:26.267 --> 00:00:29.400
I'm 33 now.
I'm an adult, you know?

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:31.167
I be doing adult stuff now.

00:00:31.167 --> 00:00:33.300
I be reading.

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:34.834
Like, for no reason,
I'll just read, like, to learn.

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:36.300
It's nice.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.868
I was reading a book on TikTok,
and it was talking about...

00:00:38.868 --> 00:00:41.033
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.033 --> 00:00:43.400
It was giving advice on how
to be a better adult.

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:44.767
It was like,
"If you're not happy with where

00:00:44.767 --> 00:00:47.234
your life is right now,
you need to start manifesting

00:00:47.234 --> 00:00:50.100
the things
you want into your life."

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:51.734
Have y'all heard about this?
Manifesting?

00:00:51.734 --> 00:00:55.767
[ Crowd cheering ]
Yeah. Women -- they love it.

00:00:55.767 --> 00:00:57.267
For the men,
if you never heard about it,

00:00:57.267 --> 00:01:01.167
it's this new thing you could do
with all your hopes and dreams.

00:01:01.167 --> 00:01:02.901
Remember back in the day
when if you wanted something,

00:01:02.901 --> 00:01:04.200
you used to have
to work to get it?

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:06.367
Remember that?
That's completely outdated.

00:01:06.367 --> 00:01:09.367
You no longer have to do that.
They've created this new thing.

00:01:09.367 --> 00:01:11.367
It's called manifesting.

00:01:11.367 --> 00:01:12.601
And the best part about it is,

00:01:12.601 --> 00:01:15.501
you don't actually
have to do anything.

00:01:15.501 --> 00:01:16.868
You just yell it out in public.

00:01:16.868 --> 00:01:19.167
That's it.
That's how I got here.

00:01:19.167 --> 00:01:20.501
I just yelled it out
on the train.

00:01:20.501 --> 00:01:21.868
"I want to be on
'The Tonight Show,'"

00:01:21.868 --> 00:01:23.634
and now I'm here.

00:01:23.634 --> 00:01:25.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:25.734 --> 00:01:27.167
Yeah, it's great.

00:01:27.167 --> 00:01:30.267
It's like a GoFundMe
for the universe.

00:01:30.267 --> 00:01:33.267
You just put it out there,
let the world pay for it.

00:01:33.267 --> 00:01:34.534
That's if you got
regular dreams, though.

00:01:34.534 --> 00:01:36.067
If you got big dreams,
there's another step.

00:01:36.067 --> 00:01:37.100
And this is a little
more complex,

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:40.567
because you've got
to get a board.

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:42.868
Y'all heard about
the vision board?

00:01:42.868 --> 00:01:44.067
If you never heard,
let me explain.

00:01:44.067 --> 00:01:45.234
It's a little more complex,

00:01:45.234 --> 00:01:47.634
because you've got
to take a day off work.

00:01:47.634 --> 00:01:48.734
You're going to go
to a hardware store.

00:01:48.734 --> 00:01:50.133
You're going to ask them
for a board.

00:01:50.133 --> 00:01:51.367
They're going to say,
"For what?"

00:01:51.367 --> 00:01:53.934
You say, "It's my dreams."
They'll understand.

00:01:53.934 --> 00:01:55.400
You're going to take the board,
you drive it home,

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:57.701
you put it on the wall
on top of your bed, right?

00:01:57.701 --> 00:01:59.934
Then you've got to step away.
And this is the important part.

00:01:59.934 --> 00:02:02.634
Now you need to find
pictures of people

00:02:02.634 --> 00:02:06.033
who have achieved the thing
you want to achieve.

00:02:06.033 --> 00:02:08.167
People that worked hard
and got after it?

00:02:08.167 --> 00:02:10.300
You're going to
find photos of them.

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:13.801
But don't do what they did.
Just the photo. That's enough.

00:02:13.801 --> 00:02:17.234
But you can't use the whole
photo, because that's stupid.

00:02:17.234 --> 00:02:20.601
You got to cut them out.

00:02:20.601 --> 00:02:22.033
And then you put them
on the board,

00:02:22.033 --> 00:02:23.734
fill up the board with photos,
and this is very important.

00:02:23.734 --> 00:02:27.467
Every night before bed,
you look at it.

00:02:29.334 --> 00:02:31.033
Then you can go to sleep.
That's it.

00:02:31.033 --> 00:02:33.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:37.400
Here's the best part.

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:38.634
If things don't
work out for you,

00:02:38.634 --> 00:02:40.200
you don't got to be embarrassed,
because

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:41.701
if things don't work out,
you can always say this.

00:02:41.701 --> 00:02:46.133
You can always say,
"It wasn't meant to be."

00:02:46.133 --> 00:02:49.667
And people understand.
It's great.

00:02:49.667 --> 00:02:52.434
Being 33 is cool because I still
feel like I'm a young guy,

00:02:52.434 --> 00:02:54.634
but I don't like doing
young-guy stuff anymore.

00:02:54.634 --> 00:02:57.367
Like, I can no longer
do the random hookups.

00:02:57.367 --> 00:02:59.734
Sorry, ladies.

00:02:59.734 --> 00:03:02.601
Because I can't spend the night
with women I just met.

00:03:02.601 --> 00:03:05.000
I used to do it in my 20s.
I could go out and meet a girl.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:06.701
We hit it off.
I go back to her place.

00:03:06.701 --> 00:03:08.501
I stay the night.
I'll stay the whole weekend.

00:03:08.501 --> 00:03:11.601
I ain't have nothing to do.

00:03:11.601 --> 00:03:14.634
She used to ask me,
"When you got to go home?"

00:03:14.634 --> 00:03:16.100
I'm like, "Thursday.
I'm going to the gym.

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:17.934
After that, I'll come back.

00:03:17.934 --> 00:03:20.467
I'm gonna do legs.
Then I'll come back."

00:03:20.467 --> 00:03:22.100
Now I can't spend the night
with a stranger.

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:23.501
And it's not even over
anything weird.

00:03:23.501 --> 00:03:25.200
It's just I'm 33 now.

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:28.167
I got to worry about sleep.

00:03:28.167 --> 00:03:29.901
Once you turn 30,
you don't just lay down

00:03:29.901 --> 00:03:31.534
and fall asleep anymore.

00:03:31.534 --> 00:03:34.601
You need to create
the perfect environment

00:03:34.601 --> 00:03:36.834
for you to get deep rest.

00:03:36.834 --> 00:03:38.634
Those are my
dating questions now.

00:03:38.634 --> 00:03:41.734
What kind of mattress you got?

00:03:41.734 --> 00:03:44.968
You got the blackout curtains?
100%?

00:03:44.968 --> 00:03:48.234
No sunlight in the morning?
That's sexy.

00:03:50.534 --> 00:03:51.634
That's who I am now.

00:03:51.634 --> 00:03:53.400
I've had beautiful women
invite me over,

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:55.834
but I take a look at them
and I'm like,

00:03:55.834 --> 00:04:00.534
"I can tell by your posture
you don't got good pillows.

00:04:00.534 --> 00:04:04.033
I need a medium firm
for my lower back, you know?

00:04:04.033 --> 00:04:05.534
And do you even have
a white-noise machine

00:04:05.534 --> 00:04:07.033
at your house?"

00:04:07.033 --> 00:04:08.367
Because I can't go
to sleep to silence, right?

00:04:08.367 --> 00:04:09.501
I need sounds.

00:04:09.501 --> 00:04:12.701
Can't do silence,
like a murderer.

00:04:12.701 --> 00:04:16.000
I need raindrops
if I'mma get rest.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:17.367
Plus, it's late.
I didn't know this.

00:04:17.367 --> 00:04:20.667
You get older, you get mad
when people invite you out late.

00:04:20.667 --> 00:04:23.200
You're like, "First of all,
it's already 6:00 p.m.,

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:25.901
and I didn't bring
any melatonin.

00:04:25.901 --> 00:04:29.167
And I know you don't have
any because you're 23.

00:04:29.167 --> 00:04:31.901
They don't sell them
the 23-year-olds, so..."

00:04:31.901 --> 00:04:33.167
Then I was getting worried.

00:04:33.167 --> 00:04:35.934
I'm like, "Am I becoming
one of these old weird men?"

00:04:35.934 --> 00:04:37.667
Then I had a conversation
with one of my boys,

00:04:37.667 --> 00:04:39.234
which, fellas,
that's what you need to do.

00:04:39.234 --> 00:04:41.033
Whenever you think
you're getting weird,

00:04:41.033 --> 00:04:44.767
talk to your boys, because then
you hear the stuff they do,

00:04:44.767 --> 00:04:47.934
and you're like,
"I'm not even that weird."

00:04:47.934 --> 00:04:49.601
I was talking to my best friend
about what happened.

00:04:49.601 --> 00:04:50.767
I was telling him -- I was like,

00:04:50.767 --> 00:04:52.400
"I can't spend the night
with women I just met.

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:54.300
Sometimes, I have
trouble sleeping, you know?

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:55.801
And I don't want her to wake up
in the middle of the night

00:04:55.801 --> 00:04:57.934
and turn over -- I'm just up."

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:02.734
These women be watching
these documentaries.

00:05:02.734 --> 00:05:04.834
I don't know what's
going through their head.

00:05:04.834 --> 00:05:05.934
And he was trying to
relate to me.

00:05:05.934 --> 00:05:07.067
He was like,
"No, I know what you mean.

00:05:07.067 --> 00:05:08.367
Same thing happened to me.

00:05:08.367 --> 00:05:09.767
I was like,
"Oh, yeah? What happened?"

00:05:09.767 --> 00:05:12.067
He was like, "One time, I was
hooking up with this girl.

00:05:12.067 --> 00:05:14.234
Middle of the night,
I accidentally took a dump

00:05:14.234 --> 00:05:15.834
in her plants."

00:05:18.367 --> 00:05:20.567
I was like,
"That's not what I mean."

00:05:22.968 --> 00:05:24.567
I thought I misunderstood.
I said, "Hold on.

00:05:24.567 --> 00:05:26.701
You actually
went in her plants?"

00:05:26.701 --> 00:05:28.000
He was like,
"You know how that go."

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:33.100
I was like, "No.
Don't include me in this."

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:35.734
Ladies, you ever wondered why
some men are so confident

00:05:35.734 --> 00:05:37.033
and where that comes from?

00:05:37.033 --> 00:05:38.467
This is where. I'll tell you.

00:05:38.467 --> 00:05:40.968
We have conversations
with our boys.

00:05:40.968 --> 00:05:42.667
They'll tell us stuff like that.

00:05:42.667 --> 00:05:46.067
We'll be like,
"Okay, I don't do that.

00:05:46.067 --> 00:05:49.200
Maybe I'm God's gift to women.

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:52.100
Is that it? Am I the best man
on the planet?"

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:54.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:55.501 --> 00:05:57.601
Then you go home
with confidence.

00:05:57.601 --> 00:05:58.968
You get into an argument
with your lady,

00:05:58.968 --> 00:06:01.467
she threaten to leave you,
but you ain't worried.

00:06:01.467 --> 00:06:03.601
You already know
what's out there.

00:06:03.601 --> 00:06:05.334
You're like,
"Where you gonna go?

00:06:05.334 --> 00:06:08.467
Find a man that's going to
ruin your plants?

00:06:08.467 --> 00:06:10.467
You don't even know what
you got. You ungrateful, okay?

00:06:10.467 --> 00:06:12.367
You need me. I'm potty-trained.

00:06:12.367 --> 00:06:15.033
You manifested this, remember?"

00:06:15.033 --> 00:06:16.601
I'm Ian Lara.
Y'all been great. Thank you.

00:06:16.601 --> 00:06:18.601
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:06:20.534 --> 00:06:21.767
-Come on, brother.
-Appreciate it.

00:06:21.767 --> 00:06:24.067
-Always. Thank you, buddy.

00:06:24.067 --> 00:06:28.801
Ian Lara! Ian Lara!

00:06:28.801 --> 00:06:33.267
See Ian this Friday
and Saturday at Laugh Boston.

00:06:33.267 --> 00:06:34.467
